                <pb facs="0322" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Argentina/142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-11T16:00:00-04:00">March 11, 1942—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. Your 403 March 3 and particularly last paragraph. The beryllium oxide
                    contract and the possible separate agreements for the purchase of other products
                    are being studied with the Reconstruction Finance Corporation but no decision
                    has as yet been reached.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
